 both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/assets/7cc5955c5268c6e933265632082a0d5be4fa87c96118b011351b71aa9ee89a7d.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=4$ is a source.\n\n- Statement III is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-1$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4535b48e-a33f-5f62-95d3-a5c0991c1f6d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Equilibrium Points Using a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95aa0559-9481-5907-b392-8993f99520e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318158} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7fa5ba-613a-531a-8c82-c7388aa1a325" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318159} {:answer/id #uuid "23cf78f2-86fc-5860-886b-6e7d97bdaa47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318160} {:answer/id #uuid "496a9117-9d71-54eb-a398-3e59f6f02cbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318161} {:answer/id #uuid "666aaf3b-15f4-5312-8d0a-a9553c537164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23cf78f2-86fc-5860-886b-6e7d97bdaa47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318160} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa9c192-a00b-5eb1-91c1-c3a73e2ffd44" :answer-field/key "selection" :